>
> For example, where is the next to the last syllable in the word
> {fe'ire'a}?
>
> How should it be pronounced?
>
> fe'irE'a or fE'ire'a or may be fe'Ire'a?


{fe'irE'a} of course. The second to last syllable is "re".
Every vowel - except {y} - is counted as one syllable.
The second to last vowel ought to be stressed.

mi'e darves

